Nature of modifications
-----------------------
Tracendroid is a security-hardening fork. The principal changes relative to
upstream Operit are:

  * Removal of the Shizuku / libsu / root / Shower / AutoGLM privileged
    execution transports and the associated ROOT/DEBUGGER permission levels.
  * A JavaScript plugin capability gate and a plugin-signature +
    trust-on-first-use verification pipeline.
  * An encrypted credential vault (EncryptedSharedPreferences).
  * A locked-down WebView for AI-generated output with a link allowlist
    (closing a remote-code-execution path), and a path-traversal fix in the
    workspace DocumentsProvider.
  * A broadcast-receiver sender allowlist and cleartext-traffic default-deny.
  * Migration of the GitHub OAuth flow from an embedded client secret to
    PKCE (RFC 7636).
  * A proot-based shell subsystem replacing the Shizuku transport.

See docs/THREAT_MODEL.md and docs/STATUS.md for the full record.


